From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:35:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Make the scoreboard thread safe

Folia shares one scoreboard between all regions but its maps had no
synchronisation, so the base patch stubbed Entity#getTeam to null,
dropped the scoreboard sent on join, stopped resetting the scores of
removed entities and unregistered /scoreboard, /team and /trigger.

Every change now holds the scoreboard monitor, so the packets it sends
reach each player in the order the changes were made. Objectives,
scores and teams live in concurrent maps, so entities read them from
any region without the monitor, and stat criteria and entity removal
skip the monitor when the board does not track them. A joining player
is sent its board whole under the monitor and only gets changes after
that, so each team and objective reaches it once.

Fixes PaperMC/Folia#25
Based on PaperMC/Folia#519 (lewisgibson)

